<%# The drawer's handle carries the same news as the roster, for the one case a
    phone cannot avoid: one screen at a time. A conversation that finished in
    another persona sits behind a shut drawer, so the count has to live where
    the drawer is opened from. Same "9+" cap as the rail, and nothing drawn at
    zero, so a quiet install looks like it always did.

    Drawn inside the handle rather than beside it, and re-rendered whenever the
    header is: the header is what the sidebar's event stream swaps out of band,
    so the number arrives with the markup around it instead of on its own.
    Written without whitespace inside, so that the empty case is really empty
    and `:empty` can hide the background. -%>
<span class="nav-badge" id="nav-badge"<% if total.to_i.positive? %> data-total="<%= total.to_i %>"<% end %>><% if total.to_i.positive? %><span aria-hidden="true"><%= total.to_i > 9 ? "9+" : total.to_i %></span><span class="sr-only"> <%= h(I18n.t("web.sessions.unread_count", count: total.to_i)) %></span><% end %></span>
